Chapter: BlitOutOfRange
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 codex-vm's bulk blit reads a guest address from cell 36160 and a length
 from cell 36168 when the guest writes command 3 to doorbell port 1296
 (tools/codex-vm.c, blit_guest_output). A pair that does not fit in guest
 RAM is refused whole and reported as a drop of the stated length. The
 address here has bit 62 set, so it lies outside any guest the vm can be
 given; 12345 is the length the report must name. The print after the
 doorbell is the control that the serial path survives the refusal.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "before"
    let a = poke-32 36160 0 0
    in let b = poke-32 36164 0 1073741824
    in let c = poke-32 36168 0 12345
    in let d = poke-32 36172 0 0
    in act
      w <- port-out-byte 1296 3
      print-line-uni ("after: " & show (a + b + c + d + w))
    end
  end
